<title>BELGIUM: Belgian BACOB bank 1996 net profit jumps 40 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian BACOB bank 1996 net profit jumps 40 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full-year 1996</p>
<p>(billions of Belgian francs, unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)	    2.97  vs	2.12</p>
<p>    Interest rate margin			  16.95  vs     13.67</p>
<p>    Commission income				4.34  vs	2.57</p>
<p>    Profit from financial transactions	 2.04  vs	2.27</p>
<p>    Total assets				 1,523.85  vs  1,188.44</p>
<p>NOTE - BACOB, an unlisted cooperative bank, is 65.6 percent held by Arcofin, a holding company controlled by the christian-democratic Arco group.</p>
</text>
